{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1082378-blood-without-a-heart","id":1082378,"title":"Blood without a Heart?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-22T13:43:07-07:00","id":1082378,"title":"Blood without a Heart?","content":"So! Heaet removal is a powerfup effect with one hell of a downside: you can't feed. Other avenues to get blood explicitly work. My question is, for someone that wants to run around without their heart all the time, what options are there?<br /> <br /> - Protean 1. Have people spill blood on the dirt.<br /> - Protean 5. Is breath stealing feeding? I could see for and against.<br /> - Oath of Fealty. Blood transfer, go.<br /> - Cruac 4 (Blood Price). Let someone else do the feeding for you, but -expensive-.<br /> - Theban 1 (Forget the name). Store vitae in a reliquary. That said, it doesnt solve the issue, it just delays it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:56:41-07:00","id":1082676,"title":"","content":"Biting Blade rite from the Blood Sorcery book.<br /> unfortunately, the only way to get blood without your heart is with Creation 4 and either Transmutation or Destruction 4.<br /> Transmutation 1 lets you use your blade instead of your fangs, and it is a mystical method of &quot;feeding&quot; as it puts it in quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T13:40:32-07:00","id":1082757,"title":"","content":"Or just use the anti-staking method of Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:34:02-07:00","id":1082791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1082378-blood-without-a-heart?p=1082757#post1082757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just use the anti-staking method of Cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> was wondering if one can use Ordo Dracul scale to remove the heart and somehow &quot;feed&quot;. The aim is to not face final death after complete body destruction not being stakeproof.<br /> Maybe Invictus oaths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T17:55:32-07:00","id":1082854,"title":"","content":"Use Protean 3 to grow a temporary heart before you fill up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:52:20-07:00","id":1083931,"title":"","content":"Protean 1: Eh. Still directed to where your body is, and not where the heart is.<br /> Protean 5: See above answer. Still feeding the heart-less body.<br /> Oath of Fealty: Yes. In my book, if the scale was performed on an Invictus as a major boon's fulfillment or as a creative way to get out of a life boon (Hey, you just helped them cheat death. Fair's fair!) then this would work. A Dragon using this... Probably not, unless you're some sort of inter-covenant liason, dual-covenant status is allowed, OR you managed to steal the secrets like a more successful Trix rabbit which has its own problems there.<br /> Cruac 4/Blood Price: Also yes. Mystical attachment to the seat of your vitae.<br /> Theban 1: ...Eh. Maaaaaaaaaaaaybe? I mean it's your heart-removed character retrieving it. But as you said, still a temporary measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:50:45-07:00","id":1083992,"title":"","content":"Theban 1 explicitly works. Vitae mystically gained and vitae previously stored in objects are the canon options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}